(defrule prompt-construction -> prompt-construction-control prompt-construction-costs prompt-construction-pipeline composer-steps prompt-construction-tiers prompt-construction-modes prompt-construction-variables prompt-construction-providers prompt-construction-caching prompt-construction-fallbacks)
(defrule prompt-construction-control -> :instruction "指示文が振る舞いの制御で果たす役割を 1 文で書く" :sample "In an LLM-based agent, the system prompt is the primary instrument of behavioral control: it encodes the agent’s identity, capability boundaries, safety constraints, and task conventions.")
(defrule prompt-construction-costs -> :evaluation-s prompt-construction-costs/costs :nucleus prompt-construction-costs/fix)
(defrule prompt-construction-costs/costs -> :instruction "全部入りの単一の指示文が持つ費用を 1 文で書く" :sample "This has two compounding costs.")
(defrule prompt-construction-costs/fix -> :instruction "その費用への対策の方針を 1 文で書く" :sample "The fix is not to trim the prompt by hand, but to make loading context-sensitive from the start.")
(defrule prompt-construction-pipeline -> :nucleus prompt-construction-pipeline/runtime-assembly :elaboration-part-whole prompt-construction-pipeline/sections)
(defrule prompt-construction-pipeline/runtime-assembly -> :instruction "指示文を実行時に組み立てる流れを 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev assembles each agent’s system prompt at runtime through the pipeline illustrated in Figure 10.")
(defrule prompt-construction-pipeline/sections -> :instruction "指示の節が持つ付随情報を 1 文で書く" :sample "Behavioral instructions are factored into independent sections, each stored as a separate markdown file and registered with two metadata fields: a condition predicate over a runtime context dictionary (None means always include), and a priority integer that controls reading order.")
(defrule composer-steps -> :instruction "組み立て役の段階を、行う順に、1 行に 1 つ段階の名前で挙げる" :frame "opendev.context-engineering.composer-step.lisp")
(defrule prompt-construction-tiers -> :instruction "標準の動作で登録する節の層を 1 文で書く" :sample "The default action-mode agent registers modular sections across five functional tiers: Core Identity for persona and non-negotiable constraints, Tool Definitions for tool-use and code-quality guidance needed during execution, Safety & Rules for conditionally loaded policies such as git conventions and task-tracking instructions, Provider-Specific Guidance for LLM-provider-specific behavioral hints, and Dynamic Context for session-specific metadata.")
(defrule prompt-construction-modes -> :instruction "推論の段階ごとに指示文が違う必要を 1 文で書く。モードごとの扱いがあれば、それも書く" :sample "Different reasoning phases require fundamentally different prompts.")
(defrule prompt-construction-variables -> :nucleus prompt-construction-variables/placeholders :evaluation-s prompt-construction-variables/indirection)
(defrule prompt-construction-variables/placeholders -> :instruction "雛形の置換の仕組みを 1 文で書く" :sample "Templates use ${VAR} placeholders resolved at render time by a PromptRenderer.")
(defrule prompt-construction-variables/indirection -> :instruction "その間接がもたらす利点を 1 文で書く" :sample "This indirection decouples template prose from tool naming: renaming a tool requires changing one registry entry rather than editing every template.")
(defrule prompt-construction-providers -> :background prompt-construction-providers/without :nucleus prompt-construction-providers/sections)
(defrule prompt-construction-providers/without -> :instruction "提供元ごとの案内が無いときに起きる問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "Without provider-specific guidance, the agent may reference capabilities it does not have.")
(defrule prompt-construction-providers/sections -> :instruction "提供元ごとの違いに、指示文の節でどう備えるかを 1 文で書く" :sample "The PromptComposer addresses this with mutually exclusive conditional sections gated on the model_provider field from the runtime environment context.")
(defrule prompt-construction-caching -> :nucleus prompt-construction-caching/two-part :evaluation-s prompt-construction-caching/savings)
(defrule prompt-construction-caching/two-part -> :instruction "入力の保存に対応する提供元への特別な分割を 1 文で書く" :sample "For providers that support input caching (currently Anthropic), the PromptComposer offers a compose_two_part() method that splits the assembled prompt into a stable part and a dynamic part.")
(defrule prompt-construction-caching/savings -> :instruction "保存の効果を、割合の見積もりで書く。値が無ければ空にする" :sample "Since the system prompt is re-sent on every LLM call and the stable portion typically comprises 80–90% of the total, caching it yields substantial cost savings over a multi-turn session (approximately 88% reduction in input token cost for the cached portion).")
(defrule prompt-construction-fallbacks -> :nucleus prompt-construction-fallbacks/skip :elaboration-set-member prompt-construction-fallbacks/monolith)
(defrule prompt-construction-fallbacks/skip -> :instruction "節のファイルが欠けたときの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "If an individual section file is missing, the composer skips it and proceeds, so the agent starts with a slightly reduced prompt rather than failing.")
(defrule prompt-construction-fallbacks/monolith -> :instruction "組み立て全体が失敗したときの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "If modular composition fails wholesale (e.g., the templates directory is absent), the builder falls back to a monolithic core template.")
